[ ] Project workspaces to the application graph in Core =v5-projection $Core emits the application graph (Decision 45), not CCO: replace the v4 projection in clearhead-core rdf/project.rs and rdf/mod.rs with the app: vocabulary in specifications/ontology.md, emitting no v4 terms. The oracle is the spec fixture: specifications/examples/conformance/graph/workspace projects to exactly expected-app.ttl and conforms to schemas/app.shapes.ttl, checked at Core's spec-conformance boundary (cargo test --all-features in clearhead-core) like the JSON schema. The platform gate (uv run --with pyshacl==0.40.1 python scripts/check-graph-shapes.py) already proves the fixture against the shapes and the CCO mapping; it does not run Core. Most of the v4 projection survives with renamed terms. Times, as of 2026-10-03 (Decisions 47, 48, 51): domain::time has Bound, Due (:) and Planned (@). As-written terms take the Bound's written form: app:plannedStart, app:plannedEnd (app:start was renamed), app:availableFrom, app:due; a date is xsd:date, a time xsd:dateTime with seconds. Derived: app:notBefore is the latest Due start over the action and its ancestors (Bound.at); app:lateFrom the earliest Due::late_from (a date's next midnight, a time itself, no grace minute); app:durationMinutes is Planned::duration in whole minutes rounded down, emitted only when at least 1. Derived instants carry an offset (the viewer's zone); @ is never inherited. Known gap: Bound's Display drops a written offset, but the spec says as-written terms keep an offset when the file wrote one; fix in Bound, not in the projection. The mapping to CCO lives in specifications/ontology/mapping (Decision 50) and is not Core's; a CCO export, if ever needed, is that mapping run as one SPARQL call, not a second structure in Rust. Measure load and query time on this workspace before and after; expect about 2x triples (v4 109 on the fixture, V5 about 175), no step change.$ !1 ^2026-10-01T20:22 #01a0faa2-7184-74d1-ae6c-1959f4af7fe3
[ ] Move the saved queries to the application vocabulary =v5-queries $Rewrite every saved query in clearhead-cli src/queries and the CLI's sparql modules against the new graph, plus this workspace's .clearhead/queries/for-human.sparql. Row shapes stay as they are, so nvim and other clients do not change; the existing query tests are the net, so freeze their expected rows before rewriting. The competency queries in ontology v5/queries are the working templates. ADDED 2026-10-01: the graph will carry no storage facts (spec convention 3, the human's call: no file paths, lines, roots or calendar ids, since another backend such as sqlite would have none). Today's rows include source_file and source_line, used by nvim to jump to source, and some index queries join through the ws:Workspace node. Keep the rows unchanged by having the implementation add locations after the query, joining each row's IRI against the loaded workspace; remove every ws: pattern from the queries. REVISED 2026-10-01 with the human: rows lose source_file, source_line and charter_root instead of the CLI adding them back; clients get locations from the new locate command. The row shapes therefore do change for those columns, and nvim moves with them (nvim-locate). RETARGETED 2026-10-02 by Decision 45: queries use the application vocabulary (the spike's view queries are the template, about a third of v4's length); file and line stay in the graph, so rows keep their location columns and nvim is unchanged. Templates: docs/history/query-surface-spike/view/{for-human,agenda,unscheduled}.rq, which already return v4's answers on the spike workspace.$ !2 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0fb02-e644-7317-88ad-1e76ecfb2b0e #01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2
[ ] Retire the v4 vocabulary everywhere =retire-v4 $Remove the v4 namespace constants and fixtures from clearhead-core, the ontology's v4 directory, examples and queries, its pytest suite and pyproject deps, and V4_DESIGN.md; point specifications/ontology.md readers at the ontology's docs/domain.md. Decide then whether clearhead.us keeps serving the v4 vocabulary for anyone holding its IRIs (cool URIs do not change) or drops it with the site.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2 #01a0faa2-71c0-7365-9b59-8baa79bf9766
[ ] Extend the graph fixture to recurring plans and objective states =v5-fixture-gaps $The graph fixture in specifications/examples/conformance/graph covers every action field and state, charters, objectives, contexts and waits, but not: an .ics recurring plan with a materialized occurrence (when/recurrence, RRULE text, occurrence as part of the recurring action), and an objective state, whose vocabulary objectives.md does not define yet (Decision 5 says objectives have state, confirmed by an agent). Settle the objective state values with the objectives-into-Core work, then add both to the workspace, expected.ttl and the shapes, with an invalid graph for each new rule. Decision 45: the gaps apply to both expected-app.ttl and expected.ttl. ADDED 2026-10-02: ontology.md's Application Graph leaves Recurrence unspecified (the recurring plan and its rule; occurrences are ordinary actions) and objective states undefined (app.shapes.ttl forbids app:state on objectives until they are). Settle both in app: terms first, then their CCO mapping.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T22:27 #01a0fb14-c5e6-73d8-9c0d-f56f11ce00a6
[ ] Show the actions that serve an objective =objective-actions-view $Moved out of the objectives action, 2026-10-01: answering it is a query (an objective's plans, then everything they contain), which V5 makes a has-continuant-part walk from the plans that name the objective. Write it as a saved query once v5-queries has moved the queries to the new graph, then surface it in the CLI and nvim like the other named queries.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T22:35 <01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2 #01a0fb1c-4455-7218-bc00-d4d38247de78
[ ] Lint empty windows and plans outside them in Core =window-lints $Decision 48 added E008 Empty Window and W015 Planned Outside the Window to specifications/linting.md (Decision 51: E008 also catches an @ block that ends at or before it starts, Planned::is_empty, and W015 compares the whole block), with example pairs in examples/linting/. Core does not implement either, and nothing in the gate consumes those examples, so no test is red: write the failing test first (from the example pairs), then the rules. E008 uses Due::is_empty over the effective window (own : intersected with ancestors'); W015 compares @ plus its duration against it. Also the older coherence warning (a local bound outside an ancestor's window) still has no code.$ !2 ^2026-10-02T18:37 #01a0ff69-2133-7a51-8986-501607134857
[ ] Move the application vocabulary's IRIs to clearhead.dev =migrate-iris $Decision 49. Replace https://clearhead.us/ with https://clearhead.dev/ for app: (vocab/app/v1#), the shapes (specifications/app-shapes, graph-shapes) and the examples, in specifications, the fixtures, the ontology's v5 files and Core's constants. Leave v4 IRIs alone: retire-v4 deletes them. Check: grep finds clearhead.us only in v4 files and history. NOTE 2026-10-03: do NOT change the context namespace UUID 0d8937ce-eb24-52d2-9532-39ea299f888b, even though ontology.md says it was derived from https://clearhead.us/context. The UUID is the constant; changing it would rename every context node. Reword the provenance sentence only.$ !2 ^2026-10-02T23:45 #01a10083-2595-77fb-9e1d-24d741f9cbed
[ ] Fold the ontology into the specification =fold-ontology $Decision 50. After retire-v4: git subtree the ontology repo's remaining v5 content, docs/domain.md and docs/DECISIONS.md into specifications/ontology/ with history; point scripts/check-graph-shapes.py and validate-pinned at the new paths; remove the ontology submodule and its CI. Proof: the pinned gate passes with one fewer submodule.$ !3 ^2026-10-02T23:45 <retire-v4 #01a10083-25a6-7683-99bc-eab755ef8171
